  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1222 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nThere is a threat of heavy rainfall and localized flash flooding \nmainly Wednesday night through Thursday night across the western and \nnorthern parts of our area. The overall pattern will be a strong \nslow moving upper level storm system moving out of the southwest US \nwith meridional south-southwest flow over the Southern High \nPlains and favorable jet stream dynamics(RRQ at 250 MB). At the \nsurface, our area will remain in the warm sector ahead of a cold \nfront through Thursday. For moisture, PW values will increase to \n1.75 to 2 inches, low level southerly flow will be advecting \ncopious amounts of low level moisture across the western part of \nthe area, and some energy from Hurricane Simon will be transported\ninto this system too.\n\nFor rainfall amounts, there is a low to medium(30-70%) chance of \n1 inch or greater west of an Abilene to San Angelo to Ozona line \nwith the highest chances of locally higher totals(2+ inches) \nacross the northwest Big Country, far northwest Concho Valley and \nCrockett County Wednesday night through Thursday night, partially\ndue to repeating rounds of thunderstorms. Also, the Day 4 and Day\n5 (ending 12Z Friday) Excessive Rainfall Outlook has slight risk \nacross much of area which means the main hazard with be localized \nflash flooding. Looks like for now, the more significant impacts \nwill just remain west and north of our area across the Permain \nBasin and South Plains into Oklahoma, but will have to watch this \nclosely as mesoscale details will play a role on the where the \nheaviest rainfall bands set up. Also, there is a low chance of an \nisolated marginal severe storm or two during this period. Please \nkeep up with the latest weather information. The Pops will be \nmedium to high chances during this event. We begin to dry out this\nweekend, as this system weakens and shears out.\n\nFor temperatures, it will be hot through Thursday and then a good \ncold front moves by Friday morning with breezy and cooler \nconditions. Highs will be in the mid 60s to lower 70s this weekend \nand lows in the upper 40s to lower 50s Sunday morning.",
